  "goodToKnow": "Die Bürgerwehr is a vigilante group or historical citizens' militia. In the 1848 revolution, many towns formed Bürgerwehren. Today, self-appointed groups patrolling streets are viewed critically, since in Germany the state holds the Gewaltmonopol (monopoly on force), and some groups have links to the far right. Sich wehren means to defend oneself. Plural: die Bürgerwehren."
